on his face and is powerfully driven sexually, occupies the middle ground 
between the two races. 
The piano is another symbol, this time of Western culture ´ sub-
limated, controlled sexual passion £ nineteenth century. Jane Campion added the piano ¯ plot because she wanted a way to explore the dawning sexuality of a repressed Victorian woman. For 
ada
, the piano is her voice, 
