over—to make it enrich rather than damage—first pinpoint exactly why ź using it. Work out precisely what your narrator is interested in and what exactly is his or her point in recounting their story. Then, instead of inserting the voice-over as you go, consciously put it aside while you plan, construct and write œ draft. When that’s done, insert the voice-over. That way, the voice-over is servant to ·, rather than vice versa. You may č tinker a bit Ñ internal content of scenes, but ế ł strong story, not just footage supporting a voice. 
