for creating a ¿ from a novel that doesn’t have one, the writer has 
three unattractive choices: first, copy the novel and write a script without a ¿; second, invent a brand new ¿; or third, angle the script so that an event of not much significance § novel becomes the ¿ (which 
¡ 156
may mean ending ­ before the novel ends, or adapting only one part 
£ novel). This can mean the novel’s message is seriously distorted. all
