eads?
The most common distractions are: repetition, redundant detail, out-of-
sequence description and intrusive ¦ voice. Distractions ı minimised by working out in advance what informati¼ reader ạ be given to be able to visualise and underst´ full import of each sequence. You ö work out the following. 
• What º sequence about?• What Â in this sequence? • What information is it vital Ã reader receives? 
The reader needs to know precisely and economically what is ēing ¼ screen § order it Â.
ś state £ characters
It may or may not be necessary to describe the characters’ ś state. û something that must be treated with caution. If the sequence is showing something not śly charged, then ī usually no ö describe emotions. 
